# Local docker configuration for the AP.RIF.Orchestrator (root compose).
# Committed to the repo as the source of truth for what env vars docker compose expects.
#
# HOW TO USE
# ----------
# 1. Rename THIS file (in this same folder — the Orchestrator root) from
#    `.env.template` to `.env`. Docker compose auto-reads `.env`.
#    You do NOT need to make a copy — just rename this one.
#    Both `.env` and `.env.local` are gitignored, so your local values stay local.
# 2. Fill in the values below.
#
# The values here are the ones the containerized backend service needs (nuget cache
# path + local DB hostname). If you only ever run `npm run docker:remote` or
# `npm run docker:fe`, you can leave these empty — the backend container is not
# started in those flows.
#
# ==========================================================================
# REQUIRED (for docker / docker:local / docker:be)
# ==========================================================================

# HOST_NUGET_CACHE
#   Absolute path on your host to a NuGet global-packages folder that already
#   has all packages the backend solution needs. Bind-mounted into the container
#   so `dotnet restore/build` runs offline (avoids corp SSL / proxy issues).
#
#   Common values on Windows:
#     C:/Users/YOURUSER/.nuget/packages
#     C:/shared/nuget-packages
#
HOST_NUGET_CACHE=

# ==========================================================================
# OPTIONAL
# ==========================================================================

# DB_SERVER_HOSTNAME
#   Only needed if `repos/AP.RTLA.Backend/AP.RTLA.Backend/AP.RTLA.Backend/appsettings.Development.json`
#   uses your machine's NetBIOS name as the SQL Server host. See the `.env.template`
#   inside the backend repo for details.
#
# DB_SERVER_HOSTNAME=MYPC

# BACKEND_PORT / FRONTEND_PORT
#   Host ports to publish services on. Defaults: 5082 / 5173. Override on collision.
#
# BACKEND_PORT=5082
# FRONTEND_PORT=5173
